--TEST--
A parameter the manifest declares a sink does not accept a tainted argument, and gives the error a `Core` sink gives, while a parameter with no declaration accepts it — `rule:security/extension-declares-sink-or-source` and `rule:security/extension-manifest-only-tightens`
--EXTENSION--
ledger
--FILE--
<?nvs
use Shop\Ledger;

tainted string $input = "a line";

// `echoString` declares nothing, so it accepts a tainted argument.
tainted string $copy = Ledger::echoString($input);

// `writeLine` declares its parameter a sink. It does not accept a tainted argument.
Ledger::writeLine($input);

// `Core\IO::remove` is a sink too, and gives the same error.
Core\IO::remove($input);
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
%A
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
